optical-depth-b2c1aea3.limits_and_boundary:
As the differential path length $ds$ approaches zero, the differential optical depth $d	au_{
u}$ also approaches zero (assuming a finite $\alpha_{
u}$), indicating negligible attenuation over infinitesimally small distances. Conversely, if the absorption coefficient $\alpha_{
